      "worked": "The line $4x-2y+5=0$ has gradient $2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2-\\frac2{x+1}\\\\y'&=\\frac2{(x+1)^2}\\\\\\frac2{(x+1)^2}&=2\\\\(x+1)^2&=1\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }-2\\\\y(0)&=0\\\\y(-2)&=4\\end{align*}$$\nAt $(0,0)$, $y-0=2(x-0)$, giving $y=2x$. At $(-2,4)$, $y-4=2(x+2)$, giving $y=2x+8$.",
